{title: To God Be the Glory}
{lyricist: Fanny J. Crosby}
{composer: William H. Doane}
{year: 1875}
{key: G}
{meta: tune TO GOD BE THE GLORY}
{meta: variation The hymn, sung to TO GOD BE THE GLORY}
{meta: license public-domain}
{meta: tags praise}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
To [G]God be the glory, great [C]things He hath [G]done;
So [G]loved He the world that He [A7]gave us His [D]Son,
Who [G]yielded His life an a[C]tonement for [G]sin,
And [G]opened the [D]life gate that [D7]all may go [G]in.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[D]Praise the Lord, praise the Lord,
[G]Let the earth hear His voice!
[D]Praise the Lord, praise the Lord,
[G]Let the people re[D]joice!
O [G]come to the Father, through [C]Jesus the [G]Son,
And [G]give Him the [D]glory, great [D7]things He hath [G]done.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
O [G]perfect redemption, the [C]purchase of [G]blood,
To [G]every believer the [A7]promise of [D]God;
The [G]vilest offender who [C]truly be[G]lieves,
That [G]moment from [D]Jesus a [D7]pardon re[G]ceives.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Great [G]things He hath taught us, great [C]things He hath [G]done,
And [G]great our rejoicing through [A7]Jesus the [D]Son;
But [G]purer, and higher, and [C]greater will [G]be
Our [G]wonder, our [D]transport, when [D7]Jesus we [G]see.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
